    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule: an owner response carries `bulkSignupWarning: true` once more than 80 owners have already been registered today (by `registrationDate`), otherwise `false`.\n\nFour files touched, kept deliberately small to minimize structural impact:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field + setter. No mapper change was needed: the project's MapStruct config uses the default (warn, not error) unmapped-target policy, so an unmapped DTO field just stays null until the responder sets it.\n\n2. **`.../function/owner/BulkSignup.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny stateless helper with one static `warned(OwnerRepository)` method. It counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals today's business day (`BusinessDay.roll(LocalDate.now())`, matching how `BuildOwner` stores it) and returns true past the threshold of 80. Isolated here so each responder change stays a one-liner.\n\n3. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** (GET) and 4. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** (POST create) \u2014 each gains an injected `OwnerRepository` and one line: `dto.setBulkSignupWarning(BulkSignup.warned(ownerRepository))`. Neither method gained a branch, so their complexity is unchanged.\n\nI put the field on both the create response (the spec's subject) and the GET response (what the test reads), so every individual owner representation reports it consistently. The entity and the mapper were left untouched.",
